      "card_ids": ["C04","C06","C07","C14","C03","C22","C31","C21"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Permeability and intestinal evidence for close ionized peptidomimetics affirmatively supports absorption-limited low F: inogatran absorptive Papp 0.34±0.07×10^-6 cm/s with higher secretory flux (C61) and human jejunal Peff 0.03×10^-4 cm/s (C65); enalaprilat jejunal Peff 0.013±0.009×10^-4 cm/s (C64); a related compound had Papp A→B <0.7×10^-6 cm/s with efflux ratio 46 (C69); pentamidine-related AP-BL Papp 1.86±1.19×10^-8 cm/s, only 4.42±0.43×10^-8 with CsA (C51, C56, C57, C59).",
      "card_ids": ["C61","C65","C64","C69","C51","C56","C57","C59"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic-clearance evidence is mixed: napsagatran, a structurally similar zwitterionic peptidomimetic, had measurable rat liver microsomal CLint 14±5.2 µl/min/mg (C85) and rat hepatocyte CLint 5±0.8 µl/min/10^6 cells (C79), supporting a possible hepatic first-pass component; however, dabigatran (also benzamidine/carboxylate) is not a CYP substrate (C77) and has low human liver microsomal glucuronidation CLint values (0.42–4.1 µL/mg/min; C74, C75, C80–C83), so hepatic metabolism is not a reliable basis for the low prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C85","C79","C77","C74","C75","C80","C81","C82","C83"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Unrelated L6 records (acetohexamide C84, compound 8b C76, compound 2r C78) are not applicable to the query and do not affect the decision.",
      "card_ids": ["C84","C76","C78"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No direct oral bioavailability measurement or fed-state-specific data exist for the query; the low prediction rests on transferable direct low-F analogs and consistent permeability/efflux evidence, so confidence remains moderate.",
      "card_ids": ["C04","C03","C21","C61","C64","C65","C69"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C74","C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80","C81","C82","C83","C84","C85"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query; the decision relies on structurally similar analogs and physicochemical priors.",
    "No fed-state-specific bioavailability, permeability, efflux, or hepatic-clearance data are available; all relevant records are from no_reported_external_condition.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability measurement exists; L6 records are for reference molecules (napsagatran in rat, dabigatran in human microsomes) and are not direct query results.",
    "No query-specific formulation or dose data are available; conventional capsule formulation worsened DX-9065a F, but no query formulation was tested.",
    "L6 intrinsic clearance values are in vitro and species/assay dependent; they cannot be converted directly into an oral F value."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low: direct human low-F amidine/carboxylate analogs (DX-9065a F=2–3%, peramivir <3%, C21 not orally viable) plus consistent low permeability/efflux evidence affirmatively support F<20%. L6 hepatic-clearance evidence is mixed—napsagatran rat clearance suggests some hepatic first-pass loss, while dabigatran human microsomal data show low hepatic metabolism—so it does not change the low prediction. Fed-state and query-specific data remain absent, so confidence is moderate."
}

